From 4167063e52d2034701af0c234c7c94dc4dfd01f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Hugo <victorhugomacedopaesleme@yahoo.com.br>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:43:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] digest: only percent-encode control codes in quoted values
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Since a2b943b115, auth_digest_string_quoted() percent-encodes every
byte >= 0x80 and not only control codes: with a signed char they are
negative and match the "< ' '" check, otherwise they match "> 0x7e".

The response hash is still calculated over the raw values and servers
do not percent-decode quoted-string values, so Digest auth fails as
soon as the username or the realm contains non-ASCII bytes, like a
realm set to "Área Restrita". SASL DIGEST-MD5 uses the same function.

Bytes >= 0x80 are obs-text and allowed in a quoted-string, so send
them as-is like before and keep encoding 0x00-0x1f and 0x7f.

Verify with test 3236.

Follow-up to a2b943b115
Fixes #23683
Closes #23684
---
 lib/vauth/digest.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/vauth/digest.c b/lib/vauth/digest.c
index 3642dc7..14530f6 100644
--- a/lib/vauth/digest.c
+++ b/lib/vauth/digest.c
@@ -155,7 +155,8 @@ static void auth_digest_sha256_to_ascii(
     curl_msnprintf((char *)&dest[i * 2], 3, "%02x", source[i]);
 }
 
-/* Perform quoted-string escaping as described in RFC2616 and its errata */
+/* Perform quoted-string escaping as described in RFC 9110, ch. 5.6.4,
+ * esp. passing %80-FF unencoded as defined for 'obs-text'. */
 static char *auth_digest_string_quoted(const char *s)
 {
   struct dynbuf out;
@@ -169,7 +170,7 @@ static char *auth_digest_string_quoted(const char *s)
       if(!result)
         result = curlx_dyn_addn(&out, s, 1);
     }
-    else if((*s < ' ') || (*s > 0x7e)) {
+    else if(((unsigned char)*s < 0x20) || (*s == 0x7f)) {
       unsigned char buf[3] = { '%' };
       Curl_hexbyte(&buf[1], (unsigned char)*s);
       result = curlx_dyn_addn(&out, buf, 3);
